Rare survivors, companions, and people trying to make it through the apocalypse alongside you. The goal is a living world, not a free army.

[b]This is an early public test of the new IsoPlayer rebuild, replacing the old zombie-shell version. Bugs and unfinished behavior are expected.[/b]

[h2]âš ï¸ Before you play[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]One extra setup step loads the Knox Java systems.[/b] Pick either method below; without one of them survivors cannot spawn.
[*]Use a fresh test save and back up any saves you care about. Old Knox survivor data is not guaranteed to carry over to this rebuild.
[*]Built and checked against Project Zomboid [b]42.20.4[/b]. Single-player is the focus; full multiplayer NPC support is not available.
[/list]

[h2]ðŸ”§ What you can test[/h2]
[list]
[*]Human NPCs with saved identities, appearances, clothing, equipment, inventories, health, and needs.
[*]Roaming, scavenging, equipment choices, eating, drinking, resting, and basic first aid.
[*]Zombie combat, melee weapons, and early firearm/reload behavior.
[*]Recruitment, companion orders, survivor groups, and early camps/base jobs and storage.
[*]Companion HUD, survivor cards, inventory interaction, and an activity feed.
[/list]
Pathing, combat, equipment choices, base work, and save/load still need real playtesting. This rebuild does not yet match every feature of the old mod. Raids, missions, and larger base systems are not being advertised as finished.

[h2]â–¶ï¸ Install and play[/h2]
1. Subscribe here and let Steam finish downloading.
2. [b]Method A (recommended, nothing to download):[/b] in Steam, right-click Project Zomboid > Properties > General > Launch Options, and paste exactly this one line:
[b]cmd /c "set JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS=-javaagent:"C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\workshop\content\108600\3749727604\mods\KnoxSurvivors\java\knox-agent.jar"=pz-game && %command%"[/b]
If Steam lives somewhere else, keep the whole line identical but swap the [b]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam[/b] part for your own Steam folder. Then just press Play in Steam.
3. [b]Method B:[/b] [url=https://github.com/exe-create/KnoxSurvivorsLauncher/releases/tag/v0.2.2-preview.1]download the Knox Survivors launcher[/url] (Windows/Linux/macOS ZIP, not Source code), extract it, and press [b]PLAY KNOX SURVIVORS[/b] each time instead of using a launch option. Do not use both methods at once.
4. In the game, enable [b]Knox Survivors[/b] in Mods and for your new save.

How to confirm it worked: after reaching the main menu, open [b]Documents\Zomboid\KnoxIsoPlayer.log[/b] and check it mentions [b]agent start[/b]. If survivors never appear and the activity feed warns the Java systems are not loaded, the launch option has a typo or Steam updated the mod mid-line: re-paste it and restart.

Steam supplies the mod and Java files together and keeps them updated; the launcher and the launch option both use the game's bundled Java. No separate Java installation is needed.

Windows is the primary test platform. Linux/macOS launcher builds pass automated checks, but real game launches on those systems still need tester reports. If the game reports the Java systems are missing, let Steam finish updating before trying again.

